<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Meaning of a Function Presented Graphically</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01385</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Meaning of a Function Presented Graphically</md:title>
    <md:uuid>db3e75be-1675-4188-81ff-7a0dd24483f6</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Here is a graph of the accumulated rainfall in Las Vegas, Nevada, in the first 60 days of 2017.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">
          <media alt="Continuous graph with title of Accumulated Rainfall, Las Vegas, Nevada, x-axis label of day of the year 2017, and y-axis label of rainfall in inches. The x-axis goes from 0 to 60 in increments of 10, the y-axis goes from 0 to 1-point-6 in increments of 0-point-2. Each day has the amount of rain accumulated with no rain in the first 10 days.">
            <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_10_02_01.png"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <para id="para-00003">Use the graph to support your answers to the following questions.</para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Is the accumulated amount of rainfall a function of time?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00005">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00006">Yes. For each number of days <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> between 0 and 60, a certain amount of rain fell up to that time, so there is one particular value for the accumulated rain at any point in time.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00007">Is time a function of accumulated rainfall?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00008">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00009">No. There was no rainfall in the first 10 days. This means that for the amount of rainfall 0 inches, or for the input value of 0, there are lots of times <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> that could be the output.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content></document>
